  "query_preview": "..\nScattered showers will be possible tonight across the Marianas, \nparticularly for Tinian and Saipan as another weak trade-wind trough\nmoves through the Marianas. Shower coverage is expected to become\nisolated again for Thanksgiving Day, but scattered showers will \nreturn Thursday night as a trade-wind surge and troughing begins to \nspread across the region. Periods of scattered showers and isolated \nthunderstorms will persist through at least Saturday night, but model\nguidance has trended downward slightly due to the upper-level \nsupport now being forecast to weaken. Ensemble guidance only suggests\n1 to 2 inches will be possible from Thursday night through Sunday. \nHave accordingly adjusted down PoPs slightly, mostly topping out as \nlow-end scattered from Thursday night through Sunday. As such, \nchances for the KBDI buster appear to be dwindling, so expect the \nKBDI to continue to slowly climb through the weekend, with today's \nvalue coming in at 608. This places us in the very high fire danger \ncategory. The aforementioned trade-wind surge will bring back higher \neast to northeast winds, from 15 to 25 miles per hour starting on \nThursday and continuing through at least Friday. Residents are urged \nto monitor any outdoor-related activities that involve a spark or \nflames, as elevated to locally critical fire weather conditions are \nongoing. Another, and potentially strong, trade-wind surge is \npossible starting Monday.",
